#---
# purpose: "clause heads decide a lane-form tuple parameter without boxing it"
#---
#
# # tuple_param_dispatch_allocations
#
# `pair/1` and `pick/1` each return a two-field tuple that reaches its consumer
# in lane form: the caller hands over one lane per field instead of a heap
# struct. The two consumers ask about that parameter in the two ways a clause
# head can.
#
# `unwrap/1` destructures it, so entry dispatch answers a tuple-arity question
# and reads field 1. `tag/1` annotates it, so entry dispatch asks a whole-value
# type question, which the predicate decomposes into one question per position.
#
# Current contract, all paths:
#
# - the arity question is decided from the parameter's transport shape, and a
#   field is a view over the lanes already in hand;
# - the annotated type question is answered per position against those same
#   lanes, so the tag routes the call without a value to read it from;
# - no struct is allocated between the two snapshots, so `struct_allocs` and
#   `struct_bytes` are both `0` on `run`, `interp`, and `build` alike.
#
# The last `unwrap/1` clause draws a `type/no-matching-clause` warning, which
# the diagnostics sidecar records.
defp pair(n), do: if n > 0, do: {n, false}, else: {n, true}
defp unwrap({v, false}), do: v
defp unwrap({_, true}), do: -1

defp pick(n), do: if n > 0, do: {:cont, n}, else: {:halt, n}
defp tag(x :: {:cont, integer}), do: 1
defp tag(x :: {:halt, integer}), do: 2

def main() do
  before = Process.heap_alloc_stats()
  a = unwrap(pair(5))
  b = unwrap(pair(-5))
  c = tag(pick(1))
  d = tag(pick(-1))
  later = Process.heap_alloc_stats()
  dbg({a, b})
  dbg({c, d})
  dbg({before[:struct_allocs], before[:struct_bytes]})
  dbg({later[:struct_allocs], later[:struct_bytes]})
end
